      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:5:2:19:7",
      "text": [
        " جَاءَ رَجُلٌ إِلَى أَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) يَدَّعِي عَلَى الْمُعَلَّى بْنِ خُنَيْسٍ دَيْناً عَلَيْهِ فَقَالَ ذَهَبَ بِحَقِّي فَقَالَ لَهُ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) ذَهَبَ بِحَقِّكَ الَّذِي قَتَلَهُ ثُمَّ قَالَ لِلْوَلِيدِ قُمْ إِلَى الرَّجُلِ فَاقْضِهِ مِنْ حَقِّهِ فَإِنِّي أُرِيدُ أَنْ أُبَرِّدَ عَلَيْهِ جِلْدَهُ الَّذِي كَانَ بَارِداً ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hammad Bin Usman, from Al Waleed Bin Sabeeh who said, ",
          "‘A man came over to Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> demanding a debt which was upon Al-Moalla Bin Khunays, so he said, ‘He has gone away with my right’. So Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> said to him: ‘It was the one who killed him that went away with your right’. Then he<sup>asws</sup> said to Al-Waleed: ‘Stand up to the man, so fulfil his right, for I<sup>asws</sup> wanted that his skin be cooled upon him which was already cold’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "7. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from al-‘ Abbas the one whom he has mentioned (in his book) who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘The Imam pays off the debts of the believing people except Muhur (dowry) of women.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
